[h2]The Boss Arena always has its boss now, and it finally pays[/h2]
[list]
[*]A player reported walking into the Boss Arena and finding it empty. It was not bad luck and it was not a spawn chance. It was three separate things stacked, any one of which empties the arena.
[*][b]The boss was spawned by a quest step, and a quest step only ever fires once per character.[/b] Soulvizier built the fight as walk into the middle, quest spawns him. Titan Quest saves that step as completed, forever. So the first visit had a boss and every visit after it was empty. He is now placed in the arena the way every other set piece boss in this mod is placed, which means the engine spawns him fresh every time the level loads: every visit, every character, no saved state involved.
[*][b]There was also a hidden character level window.[/b] The spawner was using the base game generic quest limits, which only allow the spawn between levels 29 and 36 on Normal, 41 and 55 on Epic, and 60 and 75 on Legendary. Outside that band you got nothing, with a perfectly healthy quest and monster pool sitting there. The arena now uses its own limits, levels 1 to 110, on all three difficulties.
[*][b]And the spawner was configured as quest only,[/b] with no run chance at all. It is now a world spawner at 100 percent, with exactly one Aithon guaranteed alongside his two Ember Satyr Wardens.
[*]The quest keeps everything else it did (it still opens the arena entrance); only its duplicate spawn action is gone, so there is exactly one source for the boss and you can never get two Aithons at once.
[/list]

[h2]The arena guarded nothing, and now it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Aithon carries a dedicated Boss locked chest, the [b]Ember Crowned Hoard[/b], one per kill. It opens its own loot table with a guaranteed unique plus relic slot, at the same volume as the other named boss hoards in the mod (the Tantalus chest, the Obsidian hoards, and the rest), which were all restored to their authored generosity in the previous update.
[*]The six lights ringing the arena floor now have actual flame under them, sitting on the measured floor height rather than floating.
[/list]

[i]Scope, measured rather than asserted: the world map changed in exactly one level, the arena itself, and its pathfinding data is byte for byte what it was. The quest archive changed in exactly one quest, bossarena. The database added ten records (the hoard family and the new spawn limits) and modified two (the arena spawner and its pool), and nothing else in 51,331 records moved. One new item name was added. No other boss, chest, drop rate, or area was touched.[/i]

[i]Note: the previous change note was posted against this update by mistake. It describes the Toxeus champion equipment work, which shipped in the update before this one and is unchanged here.[/i]

